{"path":"3/library/email.iterators.html","title":"email.iterators: Iterators","description":"Source code: Lib/email/iterators.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-email.iterators"},{"type":"anchor","id":"email-iterators-iterators"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"email.iterators"},{"type":"text","value":": Iterators"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/email/iterators.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/email/iterators.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iterating over a message object tree is fairly easy with the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/email.compat32-message.html#email.message.Message.walk","title":"email.message.Message.walk","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Message.walk"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method. The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"email.iterators"},{"type":"text","value":" module provides some useful higher level iterations over message object trees."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"email.iterators.body_line_iterator","term":[{"type":"text","value":"email.iterators.body_line_iterator("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"msg"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"decode"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This iterates over all the payloads in all the subparts of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"msg"}]},{"type":"text","value":", returning the string payloads line-by-line. It skips over all the subpart headers, and it skips over any subpart with a payload that isn’t a Python string. This is somewhat equivalent to reading the flat text representation of the message from a file using "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/io.html#io.TextIOBase.readline","title":"io.TextIOBase.readline","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"readline()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", skipping over all the intervening headers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"decode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is passed through to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/email.compat32-message.html#email.message.Message.get_payload","title":"email.message.Message.get_payload","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Message.get_payload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"email.iterators.typed_subpart_iterator","term":[{"type":"text","value":"email.iterators.typed_subpart_iterator("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"msg"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maintype"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"'text'"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subtype"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This iterates over all the subparts of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"msg"}]},{"type":"text","value":", returning only those subparts that match the MIME type specified by "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maintype"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subtype"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subtype"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is optional; if omitted, then subpart MIME type matching is done only with the main type. "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maintype"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is optional too; it defaults to "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"text"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thus, by default "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"typed_subpart_iterator()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns each subpart that has a MIME type of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"text/*"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following function has been added as a useful debugging tool. It should "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be considered part of the supported public interface for the package."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"email.iterators._structure","term":[{"type":"text","value":"email.iterators._structure("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"msg"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fp"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"0"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include_default"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prints an indented representation of the content types of the message object structure. For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> msg = email.message_from_file(somefile)\n>>> _structure(msg)\nmultipart/mixed\n    text/plain\n    text/plain\n    multipart/digest\n        message/rfc822\n            text/plain\n        message/rfc822\n            text/plain\n        message/rfc822\n            text/plain\n        message/rfc822\n            text/plain\n        message/rfc822\n            text/plain\n    text/plain"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fp"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a file-like object to print the output to. It must be suitable for Python’s "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#print","title":"print","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"print()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function. "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is used internally. "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"include_default"}]},{"type":"text","value":", if true, prints the default type as well."}]}]}]}]}}
